Main Tasks And Responsibilities

Noesis is looking for candidates with the following profile:


Analyze and optimize cloud spending by monitoring cloud cost data, identifying cost-saving opportunities, and driving FinOps best practices across AWS, Azure, and Google Cloud environments;
Deliver financial insights and reporting through dashboards, reports, and data analysis using Excel, Power BI, and FinOps tools to support informed business decisions;
Support budgeting and forecasting processes by providing accurate cloud cost analysis, financial forecasts, and recommendations to improve cost efficiency;
Collaborate with cross-functional teams, including Engineering, Product, Finance, and Architecture, to promote financial accountability and implement sustainable cloud cost optimization strategies.


Requirements


Degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Finance, Business Administration, or a related field;
3+ years of experience in FinOps, Cloud Cost Management, or Cloud Financial Analysis;
Solid knowledge of AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud, with a strong understanding of cloud billing and cost optimization;
Proficiency in Excel, Power BI, and cloud cost management tools;
Strong analytical mindset with the ability to transform data into business insights;
Experience working with cross-functional teams in Finance, Engineering, and Product environments;
FinOps Foundation and/or AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud certifications are a plus;
Advanced level of English.


If you meet these conditions and would like to join an innovative organization that continuously invests in training its talents, send us your application.

Join us. Let's innovate together!

All our recruitment and selection processes are based on equal opportunities, valuing the competence and potential of each person and ensuring that no candidate is discriminated on the grounds of gender, ethnicity, sexual orientation, age, religion or physical condition.
